---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy | Hipotecalc"
  description="Hipotecalc cookie policy: which cookies the site uses, for what purpose, and how to accept, reject or withdraw your consent."
  heading="Cookie policy"
  path="/en/cookie-policy"
  lang="en"
  lastUpdated="July 2026"
>
  <h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files that websites store in your browser to
    remember information about your visit, such as your preferences or
    statistical browsing data.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Which cookies this site uses</h2>
  <p>Hipotecalc uses two types of cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical cookies (necessary).</strong> They remember your
      decision about cookie consent (the <code>cookieyes-consent</code> cookie
      from the CookieYes consent manager). They do not require consent because
      they are essential to respect your choice.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics cookies (optional).</strong> These are only set if you
      expressly accept them. They are Google Analytics cookies
      (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>), which provide anonymous usage
      statistics (page views, visit duration, device type) with the IP address
      anonymised. They expire after a maximum of 2 years.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Managing your consent</h2>
  <p>
    When you first access the website, a banner lets you accept or reject
    analytics cookies. Your choice is respected on all subsequent visits and
    you can change it at any time:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      By reopening the cookie settings panel from the consent manager's icon
      or link.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you withdraw your consent, existing analytics cookies are deleted and
      are not set again.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can also delete or block cookies from your browser settings (Chrome,
      Firefox, Safari, Edge, etc.). Note that blocking technical cookies may
      prevent your preferences from being remembered.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The analytics cookies described above are set by Google Analytics. You can
    read how Google processes data in its own privacy documentation, and
    install the official Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on if you wish
    to opt out of this service on all websites.
  </p>

  <h2>5. More information</h2>
  <p>
    The processing of data collected through cookies is described in the
    <a href="/en/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
